        "original_id": "75c076dc-7c75-543d-a23c-df863587aeca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Willi Forst, Brian Robbins, H.K. Breslauer, Steven Brill\n- Films: Oh, Dear Augustine, Ready to Rumble\n- Organizations: Turner Broadcasting, World Championship Wrestling\n- Roles: actor, screenwriter, film director, film producer, singer, television director, television producer\n\nFacts:\n- Willi Forst, born Wilhelm Anton Frohs on 7 April 1903 and died on 11 August 1980, was an Austrian actor, screenwriter, film director, film producer, and singer.\n- Oh, Dear Augustine (German: Oh, du lieber Augustin) is a 1922 Austrian silent film directed by H.K. Breslauer and starring Willi Forst.\n- Brian Robbins, born Brian Levine on November 22, 1963, is an American actor, film director, film producer, television director, television producer, and occasional screenwriter.\n- Ready to Rumble is a 2000 American buddy comedy film directed by Brian Robbins and written by Steven Brill.\n- Ready to Rumble is based on Turner Broadcasting's now defunct professional wrestling promotion, World Championship Wrestling (WCW).",
